Subject: Postdoctoral inquiry — Yichao Jin (UT Dallas, Public Policy)

Dear Dr. Chandra,

I am writing to ask whether you would consider me for a postdoctoral position. I completed my PhD in Public Policy and Political Economy at UT Dallas, where my dissertation developed and validated LLM-driven digital-twin simulation for health policy — using language-model agents to scale stated-preference and behavioral experiments across heterogeneous patient populations.

Your work with Handel and Schwartzstein on behavioral economics in health-care markets has long shaped how I think about preference heterogeneity, and the recent working paper with Abdel Haq, Jagelka, Luttmer, and Schwartzstein on revealing life preferences through LLMs is essentially the validation problem I have been working on from the simulation side. I have a forthcoming digital-twin validation paper and a working paper on framing effects in LLM-simulated patient decision-making, both of which I would gladly share.

If appropriate, I would welcome the chance to discuss whether my background fits any of your current projects or the broader health policy agenda at HKS/HBS. My CV is attached; thank you for your time.

Best regards,
Yichao Jin
